@group(:core)
mod Std.Char
  ## The Unicode code point — Cure's character type.
  ##
  ## A `Char` is a Unicode scalar: an index below the code-point ceiling
  ## `0x110000` (1114112). It is `Bounded(0x110000)`, so a `Char` value is one
  ## machine integer that erases to its code point. Character literals (`'a'`,
  ## `'\n'`) elaborate to `Char` values, and a `String` is a `List(Char)`. This
  ## module gives the type its visible, documented home, mirroring
  ## `Std.Int`/`Std.Float`/`Std.Binary`/`Std.Atom`.
  ##
  ## `use Std.Char` also brings `Bounded` into scope (via `use Std.Bounded`), so
  ## a bare character literal elaborates without a separate `Bounded` import.

  use Std.Bounded

  typealias Char = Bounded(1114112)
